🚀 Feature
Implement a class (e.g. Join), child of Distribution to join/concatenate distributions of different types. This would allow to sample easily from the joined distributions, but also compute compute the log joined-probability.
For instance
>>> a, b = Uniform(0, 1), Normal(0, 1)
>>> c = Join([a, b])
>>> x = c.sample()
>>> x
tensor([ 0.7235, -1.1922])
>>> c.log_prob(x)
tensor(-1.6296)
>>> a.log_prob(x[0]) + b.log_prob(x[1])
tensor(-1.6296)
This is actually similar to Independent, but is much more versatile as it would allow to join different distribution types.
Motivation
I often work with complex parameter distributions, where some parameters are drawn from Uniform and others from MultivariateNormal. Being able to sample from such distribution with the same API as those that are already implemented would save a lot of (development) time and complexity.
Possible implementation
In sample, the events are flattened and concatenated, resulting in an output of the shape (sample_shape, batch_shape, -1).
When evaluating log_prob, the samples are split back into the respective sub-distributions and the total log probability is the sum of the individual log probabilities.
class Join(Distribution):

    arg_constraints: dict = {}

    def __init__(self, subs: List[Distribution]):
        super().__init__()

        self.subs = subs

    @property
    def mean(self):
        return torch.cat([sub.mean.view(-1) for sub in self.subs])

    @property
    def variance(self):
        return torch.cat([sub.variance.view(-1) for sub in self.subs])

    @property
    def event_shape(self) -> torch.Size:
        shape = [0]

        for sub in self.subs:
            shape[0] += sub.event_shape.numel()

        return torch.Size(shape)

    @property
    def batch_shape(self) -> torch.Size:
        return self.subs[0].batch_shape  # assume same batch_shape

    def expand(self, batch_shape: torch.Size):  # -> Join
        return Compose([sub.expand(batch_shape) for sub in self.subs])

    def sample(self, sample_shape: torch.Size = ()):
        x = []

        for sub in self.subs:
            y = sub.sample(sample_shape)
            y = y.view(sample_shape + self.batch_shape + (-1,))
            x.append(y)

        return torch.cat(x, dim=-1)

    def log_prob(self, x: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:
        i, logp = 0, torch.tensor(0.)

        for sub in self.subs:
            j = i + sub.event_shape.numel()
            y = x[..., i:j].view(x.shape[:-1] + sub.event_shape)
            i = j

            logp = logp + sub.log_prob(y)

        return logp
In this implementation, it is assumed that each sub-distribution has the same batch_shape.
